


INSTALL(1)	    UNIX Programmer's Manual	       INSTALL(1)



NNAAMMEE
     install - install binaries

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     iinnssttaallll [ --cc ] [ --mm mode ] [ --oo owner ] [ --gg group ] [ --ss ]
     binary destination

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     _B_i_n_a_r_y is moved (or copied if --cc is specified) to _d_e_s_t_i_n_a_-
     _t_i_o_n.  If _d_e_s_t_i_n_a_t_i_o_n already exists, it is removed before
     _b_i_n_a_r_y is moved.  If the destination is a directory then
     _b_i_n_a_r_y is moved into the _d_e_s_t_i_n_a_t_i_o_n directory with its ori-
     ginal file-name.

     The mode for _D_e_s_t_i_n_a_t_i_o_n is set to 755; the --mm _m_o_d_e option
     may be used to specify a different mode.

     _D_e_s_t_i_n_a_t_i_o_n is changed to owner root; the --oo _o_w_n_e_r option
     may be used to specify a different owner.

     _D_e_s_t_i_n_a_t_i_o_n is changed to group staff; the --gg _g_r_o_u_p option
     may be used to specify a different group.

     If the --ss option is specified the binary is stripped after
     being installed.

     _I_n_s_t_a_l_l refuses to move a file onto itself.

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     chgrp(1), chmod(1), cp(1), mv(1), strip(1), chown(8)

























